      "text": "\n\nHere's my honest assessment of your app's current aesthetic and some suggestions:\n\n---\n\n**What's working well:**\n- **Dark theme** — The deep navy (`#0A1628` → `#0F2847`) palette feels appropriate for a mountaineering app. It gives an \"expedition at night\" vibe.\n- **Category color coding** — Gold for 7 Summits, red for 8000m, green for 14ers — this is intuitive and adds visual variety.\n- **Card press animation** — The spring scale on MountainCard is a nice micro-interaction.\n- **Profile dashboard** — The stats grid, progress bars, and difficulty breakdown are well-structured and information-dense without being cluttered.\n\n---\n\n**Where it could improve:**\n\n1. **It feels a bit \"flat and samey\"** — Almost everything is `cardBg` (#122240) rectangles on a `primary` (#0A1628) background. There's not enough visual contrast between sections. Consider:\n   - Adding subtle gradient cards for hero elements (like \"Highest Summit\")\n   - Using slightly different card treatments (e.g., a frosted/glassmorphism card for the completion progress)\n   - Adding a background texture or subtle topographic pattern\n\n2. **The accent color (`#4DA8DA`) is safe but forgettable** — It's a generic blue that doesn't evoke mountains. Consider a warmer accent like an alpine sunrise orange/amber, or an icy teal-green that feels more specific to the outdoors.\n\n3. **Typography could be bolder** — You're using system fonts at reasonable sizes, but the hierarchy could be stronger. The title \"Summit Tracker\" at 28px and card names at 15px don't create enough drama. Consider a larger, more expressive title treatment, or a condensed weight for elevation numbers.\n\n4. **No imagery or atmosphere** — The app is purely text + icons. Even without custom assets, you could add:\n   - Gradient overlays that shift color based on elevation (warmer at low, cooler/icier at 8000m+)\n   - A subtle SVG mountain silhouette behind the header\n   - Elevation-based visual cues on cards (a thin gradient strip showing altitude color)\n\n5. **The empty state is underwhelming** — Just a gray icon + text. This is your first impression for new users. A more inspiring empty state with an illustrated mountain scene and motivational copy would set the tone.\n\n6. **Cards are information-dense but lack personality** — Every card looks the same. Consider differentiating visually by difficulty or category — e.g., \"Extreme\" peaks could have a subtle red glow or different border treatment.\n\n---\n\n**Vibe suggestions to consider:**\n\n| Direction | Feel | Colors |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| **Alpine Dawn** | Warm, aspirational | Deep charcoal + warm amber/gold accents + soft peach highlights |\n| **Ice & Stone** | Rugged, serious | Slate gray + ice blue + stone white + muted teal |\n| **Expedition Log** | Vintage, journal-like | Warm dark brown + cream/parchment tones + burnt orange |\n| **Neon Summit** | Modern, techy | Black + electric green/cyan accents (like a Garmin watch) |\n\n---\n\nWant me to implement any of these directions, or tweak specific parts of the design? I can rework the color palette, add atmosphere to the header, improve card treatments, or go for a full visual refresh.",
